1. Write some codes in app.py --> In Treminal [python app.py]
2. Create a "requirements.txt" file
3. Create a file named "dockerfile" and add content in it. [For Creating An Image Of Docker With All The things like: OS, Dependencies, Codes, virtual-Env, Programming-Language.]
4. Run code [docker build -t <name-u-want> . (docker build -t docker-demo .)] {Ye likhne se "image" wale tab me jayega docker-desktop ke}
5. Build an docker Image run command on powershell or VScode Terminal Both [docker run -p 5000:5000 <name-u-want> (docker run -p 5000:5000 docker-demo {same upar wala})] {Ye likhne se "container" wale tab me jayega docker-desktop ke}


Notes: yaha 5000:5000 [Jo pehla 5000 hai, wah hamare docker image ka port hai jo humne apne "dockerfile" me likha hai "EXPOSE 5000", Aur dusra 5000 hamare "Stytem" ka port hai ]




Below-Commands We Can Execute From VSCode Terminal OR, Docker-Desktop Terminal OR Power-Shell All Three.

6. Tag Your Image: docker tag <project-name> user-name/<project-name>:latest1 [docker tag docker-demo akkukumar1234/docker-demo:latest1]
7. Push Image To DockerHub: docker push user-name/<project-name>:latest1 [docker push akkukumar1234/docker-demo:latest1]

8. Pull Image From DockerHub: docker pull user-name/<project-name>:latest1 [docker pull akkukumar1234/docker-demo:latest1]

9. Run The Pulled Image: docker run -p 5000:5000 user-name/<project-name>:latest1 [docker run -p 5000:5000 akkukumar1234/docker-demo:latest1]


Jab hume docker-hub se docker image lakar run karna ho

In The Docker Terminal
1. docker pull <repo-name> [Docker Desktop Ke "Image" Tab Me Jayega]
2. docker run <repo-name> [Docker Desktop Ke "Container" Tab Me Jayega]


Jab Pura Kam Khatm Ho Jayega Tab, Hume Ise Github Pe Push Kar Dena Chahiye